is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: web_server_1
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: Application layer (Apache on web_server_1) – HTTPS/TLS virtual host and listener are not configured.
Mechanism: The user’s bookmark hits https://web1.local. Because Apache on web_server_1 only listens on port 80 (HTTP) and does not have a TLS listener on 443, the TCP connection for HTTPS cannot be established, so browsers report a hang/timeout. Plain HTTP works, which is why http://web1.local loads instantly.
Localization: On web_server_1 (10.200.0.4), netstat shows only 0.0.0.0:80 LISTEN and no 443 listener. From host_1_1_1_1: HTTP to http://web1.local returns 200 OK (Apache/2.4.62) with fast times; HTTPS to https://web1.local fails (curl http_code=000). DNS resolves web1.local to 10.200.0.
[FINAL] stop=no-more-tool-calls tool_calls=16
